    pr_ref:  # 78e0
    description: "Machine became unresponsive (SSD at 2 Gbps, swap thrashing) after 56 days of uptime. Root cause: background bakeoff analyzing vscode (3.3GB) + pytest -n auto (6 workers × ~1GB each) = ~9GB from hypergumbo alone, exceeding available memory on 22GB/512MB-swap machine.\n\nMechanical prevention needed — 'trying harder' is not a solution. Options:\n1. Memory limit per analysis process (ulimit -v or cgroup)\n2. Bakeoff memory check: read free memory before launching, skip/queue large repos if below threshold (e.g., 4GB free minimum)\n3. Cap pytest parallelism during bakeoffs (smart-test could check for running bakeoff PIDs)\n4. Add max-memory flag to hypergumbo run that aborts if RSS exceeds limit\n\nPriority P2 because this crashed the machine and required hard reboot."  # 78e0
    fields: {}  # 78e0
